\section*{Absolute Continuity Parameters for Bernoulli Convolutions}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
Unbiased Bernoulli convolutions are claimed to admit an arithmetic singularity criterion for every parameter, with singular reciprocal quartic-Salem and specified degree-31 non-Pisot examples. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 153, 2026-10-03): Measure concentration supplies finite bit-word differences whose initial coefficients can be completed to height-one polynomials with roots just above the parameter. Uniform finite-order nonvanishing retains the sign change, and irreducibility over the two-element field is imposed without changing the initial data, converting overlap concentration into one-sided algebraic-unit approximation.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 153, 2026-10-03): The independently defined finite algebraic-unit sets specify an explicit limsup approximation set C; the classification theorem states singular iff lambda belongs to C and absolute continuity iff not, covering every lambda in (0,1). A finite decision algorithm is not required by this record.

\subsection{Formal verification}
Family 153 has no Lean scope page in this snapshot; no formalization of these manuscript results is listed.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item OpenAI, \emph{Arithmetic classification and non-Pisot singularity for Bernoulli convolutions}, 2026-10-03; citation key \texttt{OAI:Arithmetic-classification-and-non-Pisot-singularity-for-Bernoulli-convolutions-October-3-2026}. \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Arithmetic-classification-and-non-Pisot-singularity-for-Bernoulli-convolutions-October-3-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (GitHub)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/raw/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Arithmetic-classification-and-non-Pisot-singularity-for-Bernoulli-convolutions-October-3-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (direct)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Arithmetic-classification-and-non-Pisot-singularity-for-Bernoulli-convolutions-October-3-2026/README.md}{Manuscript page and citation}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/Arithmetic-classification-and-non-Pisot-singularity-for-Bernoulli-convolutions-October-3-2026/paper.pdf}{Latest version}.
